# Walkthrough - Enhanced Timetable Events

I have significantly improved the timetable event system, moving from a basic title-only prompt to a full-featured management system.

## Changes Made

### Frontend Enhancements
- **New Event Modal**: Replaced the simple prompt with a dedicated [EventModal](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/timetable/EventModal.tsx#29-191) component.
    - **Duration Support**: Users can now set specific start and end times for events.
    - **Categories**: Added support for 'Study', 'Meeting', 'Personal', and 'Deadline' categories.
    - **Visual Cues**: Each category has a dedicated icon (Book, Users, Alert, etc.) and a consistent color scheme.
    - **Editing**: Clicking an existing event now opens the modal for modification or deletion.
- **Styling Fix**: Resolved a build error in [globals.css](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/globals.css) where an unknown `glass` utility was being applied incorrectly.

### Backend Updates
- **Update Endpoint**: Added `PUT /api/v1/timetable/events/{event_id}` to support modifying existing events.
- **Routing Fix**: Identified and removed a stale `.pyc` file that was causing `405 Method Not Allowed` errors on the new routes.

